-- title:
--   Existence of an adelic lift for Γ₁(M) cusp forms of weight two
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a non-zero natural number and let $g$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(M)$. The assertion is that there exists a function $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ (that is, on [`AutomorphicForm.AdelicGL2 (NumberField.RingOfIntegers ℚ) ℚ`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L12), the general linear group of degree $2$ over `AdeleRing (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ`) with values in $\mathbb{C}$ satisfying the three conditions packaged by [`CuspForm.IsAdelicLiftOfGamma1`](def/CuspForm_AdelicLiftGamma1.html#L14): first, $\varphi(\iota(\gamma)x) = \varphi(x)$ for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$ and every adelic $x$, where $\iota$ is the map [`AutomorphicForm.globalPoints`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L15) induced on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ by the structure map $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}$; second, $\varphi(x\,\mathrm{finEmbed}(u)) = \varphi(x)$ for every $x$ and every $u$ in the subgroup [`NumberField.AdelicLevel.finiteLevelOne`](def/NumberField_AdelicLevel.html#L418) of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles attached to the ideal [`AdelicDock.ratLevel M`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L303) generated by $M$ in $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, consisting of those $u$ for which both $u$ and $u^{-1}$ satisfy the predicate `IsLevelOneMatrix` at that ideal, with [`AdelicDock.finEmbed`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L145) the induced homomorphism from $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles to $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles; and third, for every adelic $h$ whose finite component [`NumberField.AdelicLevel.glFin`](def/NumberField_AdelicLevel.html#L194) of $h$ is the identity and whose real matrix [`LanglandsTunnell.ratArchGL2`](def/LanglandsTunnell_DeltaLift.html#L16) $h$ — obtained from the archimedean component of $h$ at the infinite place of $\mathbb{Q}$ through the identification of its completion with $\mathbb{R}$ — lies in $\mathrm{GL}_2^{+}(\mathbb{R})$, one has $\varphi(h) = (g \mid_{2} \mathrm{ratArchGL2}(h))(i)$, the weight-$2$ slash of $g$ evaluated at the point $i$ of the upper half-plane.
--
--   This is the classical passage from a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ to the associated function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$, left invariant under the rational points and right invariant under the level-$M$ compact open subgroup of the finite adelic points, normalised by its values on the archimedean points of positive determinant. It is used downstream in the construction of primitive adelic forms attached to newforms.
